round":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":28,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"## Findings\n\nI reproduced the failure locally (`compileTestJava` with `GVM_TCK_LV=8.0.0.Beta1`) and confirmed it's not a code-generation problem — it's a real Gradle dependency-resolution conflict, verified in an isolated scratch project outside the repo:\n\n- `org.hibernate:hibernate-spatial:8.0.0.Beta1` is a plain Maven-POM relocation to `org.hibernate.orm:hibernate-spatial:8.0.0.Beta1`.\n- Starting with **8.0.0.Beta1**, Hibernate began publishing Gradle Module Metadata (`.module`) for `org.hibernate.orm:hibernate-spatial`, which declares it also provides the capability `org.hibernate:hibernate-spatial:8.0.0.Beta1` (for back-compat).\n- Gradle now sees two distinct components both claiming that same capability/version (the plain relocation POM vs. the aliased capability in the `.module` file) and fails with \"Cannot select module with conflict on capability ... also provided by [...]\".\n- `8.0.0.Alpha1` (already tested successfully) had **no** `.module` file for `org.hibernate.orm:hibernate-spatial`, so the conflict didn't exist yet — this is a new upstream packaging change in Beta1, not a native-image or reflection issue.\n- I verified a working fix: adding a `resolutionStrategy.capabilitiesResolution` rule (selecting the `org.hibernate.orm:hibernate-spatial` candidate for the `org.hibernate:hibernate-spatial` capability) resolves cleanly, without touching the existing `testImplementation \"org.hibernate:hibernate-spatial:$libraryVersion\"` line. Adding it as a plain extra dependency, or excluding the platform, did **not** fix it.\n\nThis isn't a Native Image unsupportability case at all — it never reaches compilation of reflective/dynamic-access code; it fails at Gradle dependency graph resolution due to upstream POM/module-metadata packaging.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"advisory_preparation\",\n  \"summary\": \"8.0.0.Beta1 is the first hibernate-spatial release published with Gradle Module Metadata that aliases the org.hibernate.orm:hibernate-spatial capability back onto org.hibernate:hibernate-spatial, which collides with the plain-POM relocation artifact under the same old coordinate; Gradle cannot resolve the resulting capability conflict without an explicit capabilitiesResolution rule.\",\n  \"deterministic_setup\": [],\n  \"agent_guidance\": \"Keep the generated `testImplementation \\\"org.hibernate:hibernate-spatial:$libraryVersion\\\"` dependency as-is, but add a capability resolution rule to the test project's build.gradle so Gradle picks the org.hibernate.orm variant instead of failing on the capability conflict introduced by 8.0.0.Beta1's Gradle module metadata:\\n\\nconfigurations.all {\\n    resolutionStrategy.capabilitiesResolution.withCapability(\\\"org.hibernate:hibernate-spatial\\\") {\\n        def ormCandidate = candidates.find { it.id instanceof ModuleComponentIdentifier && it.id.group == 'org.hibernate.orm' && it.id.module == 'hibernate-spatial' }\\n        if (ormCandidate != null) {\\n            select(ormCandidate)\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nVerified in an isolated scratch Gradle project (not in this repo) that this rule alone turns the failing compileClasspath/testCompileClasspath resolution into a clean one; plain extra testImplementation dependencies or excludes do not fix it.\",\n  \"risks\": [\n    \"This is an upstream Hibernate packaging regression specific to how 8.0.0.Beta1 was published (Gradle module metadata added for org.hibernate.orm:hibernate-spatial with a self-conflicting capability alias); 8.0.0.Alpha1 had no such .module file and was unaffected. Future 8.0.0 releases should be re-checked to see if Hibernate keeps this capability aliasing or fixes it upstream.\",\n    \"The fix was verified only in an isolated scratch project against Maven Central metadata, not against this repo's actual testCompileClasspath/nativeImageTestClasspath configurations — local Gradle/Native Image verification in this repo should confirm the rule applies cleanly there too.\"\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":12792,"type":"result","duration_ms":290504,"uuid":"82949af4-14d2-4cc6-8f54-b7a843290fb1","ttft_stream_ms":4226,"time_to_request_ms":2306,"first_content_frame_ms":4227,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}

